            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi! I don't think so, mostly because it has two personal \"red flags\" (i.e. not red flags per se, but red flags for me personally when it comes to this type of decision):\r\n- Heavily uses tree-sitter.\r\n- Requires tracking and maintaining per language data (queries).\r\n\r\nSo the answer is \"probably not\".",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi! I don't think so, mostly because it has two personal \"red flags\" (i.e. not red flags per se, but red flags for me personally when it comes to this type of decision):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Heavily uses tree-sitter.</li>\n<li>Requires tracking and maintaining per language data (queries).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So the answer is \"probably not\".</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hi! I don't think so, mostly because it has two personal \"red flags\" (i.e. not red flags per se, but red flags for me personally when it comes to this type of decision):\n\nHeavily uses tree-sitter.\nRequires tracking and maintaining per language data (queries).\n\nSo the answer is \"probably not\".",
